{"availability":"available","full":"nalinbhardwaj/shiit-coin","name":"shiit-coin","description":"Putting a blockchain on Google Sheets 🤡","category":"Finance","language":"JavaScript","stars":120,"forks":2,"created":"2021-05-27T06:42:52Z","updated":"2021-09-26T23:57:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://shiit-coin.vercel.app","topics":["blockchain","dapp","defi"],"demo":"https://shiit-coin.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:34.417Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:34.417Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:34.417Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:08:34.417Z","stars":120,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Some ideas are bad, and then sometimes there are ideas so bad they actually go back around to being genius — we think we've come across one of those. Yes! We have an end to end blockchain working entirely off of a google sheet: transaction broadcasting, mining, wallets, gossip — all of it!","ShiitCoin is (obviously) a troll project not meant to be rEaL mOnEy 💴 but we’re hoping to farm some internet points there’s some educational value to exploring the barebones of a blockchain which we’ll share here. But first, let's talk about our adventure starting from bets on slack chat to this masterpiece of DeFi.","The origins of this project were humble, we started in our fictional garage (as coworkers at a startup) and faced a very practical problem: we made KitKat bets with each other about the most random things, and we wanted a “secure” way to maintain this ledger."],"features":["Google Apps Script lets you write real JS code that can interact with Google Sheet with Google auth from the user (and pretty much everything else).","Google Sheets has a concept of protected sheets where you can “lock” a sheet and make it so only you are allowed to write to it and restrict everyone else to read-only access (err, except the sheet creator, but let's…","Apps Script supports time triggers which allows your script to run on a regular schedule. This allows clients to run miners and gossip scripts hands-free."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nalinbhardwaj/shiit-coin/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7b2f20ddaae24e75284654c1ab084e74b3a120b60fe101d99a9c8f25e2a86713","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:34.541Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:34.541Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Some ideas are bad, and then sometimes there are ideas so bad they actually go back around to being genius — we think we've come across one of those. Yes! We have an end to end blockchain working entirely off of a google sheet: transaction broadcasting, mining, wallets, gossip — all of it!","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nalinbhardwaj/shiit-coin/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"7b2f20ddaae24e75284654c1ab084e74b3a120b60fe101d99a9c8f25e2a86713","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nalinbhardwaj/shiit-coin/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:34.542Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2021-09-26T23:57:01Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nalinbhardwaj/shiit-coin/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:34.542Z","hash":"7b2f20ddaae24e75284654c1ab084e74b3a120b60fe101d99a9c8f25e2a86713","originalBytes":11458,"storedBytes":11458,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["google","script","how","sheet","transaction","apps","blockchain","other","private","chain","gossip","key","there","mining","out","were","what","make","much","sheets","shiitcoin","using","which","block","each","every","ideas","put","run","some","transactions","work","about","allows","any","btc","client","clients","difficulty","eth","figure","idea","implement","just","node","one","only","own","proof","public","real","sequence","sheet.","sign","support","their","these","very","wallets","way","account","back","between","blocks","came","centralisation","chains","complicated","computation","